>speech_prog both~
if quest(22,5,$n) == 2
  say Ahhh... yesss...
  say You would obviously walk past the gold and then
  say check around to see if it is some kind of trap,
  say after disposing of the would-be trapper you would
  say come back and retrieve the gold for yourself.
  grin
  say $n You are on your way to becoming truly evil, but I
  say warn you I will not tolerate any more wrong answers.
  say You must prove your desire to me in other ways than
  say answering my petty questions.
  say Are you ready for what I have to ask of you?
  mpmset $n quest 22 5 3
endif
~
>speech_prog p i am ready~
if quest(22,5,$n) == 3
  say The good people of the realms must perish
  say Destroy Corwin and bring me that which he wears
  say upon his shoulders.
  mpmset $n quest 22 5 4
endif
if quest(22,5,$n) == 5
  say Defeat Caine and bring me that which he wears upon
  say his chest.
  mpmset $n quest 22 5 6
endif  
if quest(22,5,$n) == 7
  say Kill Arcus and bring me his infamous weapon.
  mpmset $n quest 22 5 8
endif
if quest(22,5,$n) == 10
  say Good luck then.
  mpgoto 11392
  mppurge all
  mpmload 11325
  if class ($n) <= 3
    mpoload 11337
    mpoload 11338
    drop all
  else
    mpoload 11339
    mpoload 11340
    drop all
  endif
  if class ($n) >= 4
    mpoload 11341
    drop all
  else
    mpoload 11342
    drop all
  endif
  mpgoto $n
  mpoload 11336
  mpquiet on
  cast "giant strength" $n
  mpquiet off
  give wits $n
  mpat 11392 mpforce $n help help_mist1
  mptransfer $n 11392
  mpat 11392 mpforce $n look
  tell $n Your wits are your strongest asset.
  tell $n Use them first.
endif
if quest(22,5,$n) == 16
  say Well $n, Your final test will be to defeat me in battle.
  say Go now and prepare.  I warn you though.
  say Next time you set foot before me may very well be your last. 
  cackle
  say I will see you again in the fervor pitch of battle.
  mpmset $n quest 22 5 17
endif
